{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>And you shall see</b> — [this is] a form serving in place of another [i.e., a substitute root]. Likewise is <i>and you shall see</i> (על ישראל שלום וראה) in 'peace upon Israel.'"], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 128, :notes {0 "Ibn Ezra argues that וראה here derives from a different root than ordinary 'seeing.' The cross-reference is to Psalms 125:5, where the phrase is ושלום על ישראל; the lemma וראה does not appear there in the received text, so the citation may reflect a variant reading or a paraphrastic gloss."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:41:26.667776009Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}